<title>FINLAND: HANDELSBANKEN LOWERS MARKKA PRIME RATE.</title>
<headline>HANDELSBANKEN LOWERS MARKKA PRIME RATE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Handelsbanken said in a statement on Monday it had decided to lower its Finnish reference rate to 4.20 percent from 4.25 percent on September 16.</p>
<p>It cited a favourable inflation outlook, the Bank of Finland tender rate cut to 3.25 percent, low market interest rates and a stable markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
